{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And HaShem set a sign for Cain</b> — And Scripture did not say 'and HaShem gave him a sign' or 'and He made,' which teaches that He set for him a fixed sign that would be with him always. Perhaps, as he traveled from place to place, there would be for him a sign from HaShem indicating the road on which he should walk, and by this he would know that no harm would befall him on that road. And in Bereshit Rabbah (Genesis Rabbah 22:12) they said something of this sort: Rabbi Abba said, He gave him a dog. For since his fear was of the wild beasts, He gave him one of them to walk before him, and to whatever direction the dog turned to walk, he would know that there HaShem had commanded for him, and he would not be killed there. The Sages mentioned in it a lowly sign, as befits him, but the intention is that the sign was with him always to show him the way he should walk, for such is the force of 'and He set':"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:24:37.762656329Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}